---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Example from '../components/Example.astro';
import CodeViewer from '../components/CodeViewer.astro';
import {version,releaseUrl,releaseArchiveUrl,npmPublished,development} from '../data/release.js';
import ReleaseStatus from '../components/ReleaseStatus.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const sections=[{id:'install',title:'Get the files'},{id:'first-page',title:'Your first page'},{id:'page-defaults',title:'Page defaults'},{id:'scoped',title:'Scoped use'},{id:'next',title:'Next steps'}];
---
<DocsLayout title="Get started" active="guide" sections={sections}>
<p class="doc-kicker">LEARN</p><h1>Get started</h1>
<p class="doc-lead">RevaCSS styles native HTML and adds a small set of classes for component patterns. Your application does not need browser JavaScript or a CSS build step to use the generated files.</p>
<section id="install"><h2>1. Get the stylesheets</h2>
{!development ? <><p><strong>Recommended: download the compiled starter.</strong> Unzip the <a href={releaseArchiveUrl}>RevaCSS {version} ZIP</a> and open <code>starter.html</code>. The archive includes its <code>dist/</code> stylesheets, fonts and icons. No package manager or build step is needed.</p>
<div class="row"><a class="button" href={releaseArchiveUrl}>Download starter ZIP</a><a href={releaseUrl}>Release notes and checksums</a></div></> : <p>This version is in development. Download the documentation stylesheet for experimentation, or build from source using the instructions below. Versioned GitHub downloads appear here after release publication is verified.</p>}
<p>For an existing site, copy <code>dist/</code> into your public assets and update the stylesheet path. Start with <code>reva.css</code>; <code>reva.min.css</code> is the minified equivalent. Fonts are optional: using <code>reva-fonts.css</code> also requires its adjacent <code>fonts/</code> directory.</p>
{npmPublished && <><h3>Install with npm</h3><CodeViewer id="npm-install" label="Install the published RevaCSS package" lang="bash" code={`npm install revacss@${version}`}/><p>In a CSS-capable bundler, import <code>revacss</code>. For a plain HTML page, use the versioned CDN stylesheet:</p><CodeViewer id="cdn-install" label="Load RevaCSS from a versioned CDN" code={`<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/revacss@${version}/dist/reva.min.css">`}/></>}
<details class="doc-summary"><summary>Build the stylesheets from source</summary><p>For contributors who want to edit the framework’s CSS or design tokens:</p>
<CodeViewer id="build-files" label="Build the distributable files" lang="bash" code={'git clone https://github.com/eristavi/RevaCSS.git\ncd RevaCSS\nnpm ci\nnpm run build:css'}/>
</details>
<p>You can also <a href={base+'reva/reva.css'} download="reva.css">download this documentation build’s stylesheet</a> for experimentation. Use a versioned release when deploying your own site.</p><ReleaseStatus/></section>
<Example id="first-page" title="2. Create a page" description="Save this complete example beside the downloaded dist directory. Native buttons need no component class; card and container identify layout patterns." render={false} html={'<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en" data-theme="auto" data-palette="default">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="utf-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">\n  <title>My RevaCSS page</title>\n  <link rel="stylesheet" href="dist/reva.css">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class="container">\n    <h1>Your projects</h1>\n    <article class="card">\n      <h2>First project</h2>\n      <p>Start with native content.</p>\n      <button type="button">Save changes</button>\n    </article>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>'}/>
<Example id="page-defaults" title="3. Configure the parent" description="Settings on html supply defaults for supported descendants. Omit anything you do not want to change." render={false} html={'<html lang="en" data-theme="dark" data-accent="violet"\n      data-shape="rounded" data-density="comfortable">\n  <!-- Components inherit these appearance settings. -->\n</html>'}/>
<p>Keep attributes on the parent where possible. Individual exceptions can override one setting without replacing the others. See <a href={base+'guide/styling/'}>styling and inheritance</a> before adding configuration to every component.</p>
<Example id="scoped" title="4. Style part of an existing site" description="Load the scoped build instead of the global build. Put configuration on its .reva boundary; each boundary starts with its own defaults." render={false} html={'<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/reva/reva.scoped.css">\n<section class="reva" data-theme="dark" data-accent="teal">\n  <h2>A styled part of the page</h2>\n  <button type="button">Save changes</button>\n</section>'}/>
<p>A CSS scope is not Shadow DOM isolation. Keep overlay markup within its boundary and use the matching scoped glass extension when needed.</p>
<section id="next"><h2>Where to go next</h2><ul>
<li><a href={base+'guide/motion/'}>Configure scrolling, overlays and disclosure motion.</a></li>
<li><a href={base+'guide/effects/'}>Understand surfaces, selection and validation feedback.</a></li>
<li><a href={base+'guide/modern-css/'}>Explore modern CSS patterns with native fallbacks.</a></li>
<li><a href={base+'themes/'}>Pick a colour mode and optional material.</a></li>
<li><a href={base+'components/forms/'}>Use native form markup.</a></li>
<li><a href={base+'reference/'}>Look up exact files, attributes and component APIs.</a></li>
<li><a href={base+'guide/accessibility/'}>Understand native behaviour and application responsibilities.</a></li>
</ul></section>
</DocsLayout>
